    slot_2_summary:S485 built p11_alt_embeddings.py multi-embedding evaluator (residue-class Phi_R(n;q)=(n mod q, n//q) and polynomial-image Phi_Q(n;q)=(n, n^2 mod q)). Tested at N in {10^4, 10^5, 10^6}, prime moduli p in {2,3,5,7,11} and primorial moduli q in {6,30,210,2310}. Findings: (i) Prime modulus p: L_p = L_r exactly (constant in N) for both embeddings — primes saturate the embedding's quotient. (ii) Primorial q with q^2 << N (column-dominated): wheel-sieve compression observed. residue ratio = phi(q)/q + small (q=30:0.30, q=210:0.233); poly ratio = (1/2)*prod_{p|q,p>2}(p-1)/(p+1) + small (q=210:0.188, q=2310:0.118). (iii) Primorial q with q^2 > N (row-dominated): residue compression collapses to ratio=1 (one horizontal per row). poly_q is row-immune and retains compression. Top-line CSV confirms: residue lines = phi(q) coprime classes + small primes; poly lines = coprime QR cosets. Conclusion: line-cover compression is exactly the wheel sieve geometrically realised. Optimal q=sqrt(N) gives ratio ~ 1/log(N). No incidence-geometric structure beyond classical density theory. B-grade. Slot 3 next.
