y polylog-time algorithm enumerating dominant slope-±1 HL diagonals + outputting fractional cover within ε of LP, not pursued by Thread 11. **Five falsifiers**: (F1) c may slowly vary with N rather than being asymptotic constant — testable at N=10⁷-10⁸; (F2) ⟨θ⟩_LP ≈ 1.42 inferred from one decomposition, asymptotic stability not proven; (F3) closed-form for c may exist via deeper joint-HL theory; (F4) alternative embedding (rotated spiral, hex-spiral, custom) might give different c; (F5) bipartite-LP analytic theory not exhausted — possibly c expressible via singular-series mixture under sharper assumptions. **Cites**: E1.5 (compression floor, primes), Hardy-Littlewood Conjecture F (cross-domain primary, from CROSS_DOMAIN_TECHNIQUES.md), Stanley 1989 matroid LP (S486 cross-domain), Singh-Lau / Lavi-Swamy iterated rounding (S487 cross-domain), Szemerédi-Trotter incidence theorem (off-edge background). **Cross-domain ingredients**: HL Conjecture F applied to slope-+/-1 quadratic-prime sequences (4k²+bk+γ form) — first incidence-geometric application in the project. **Closure mode**: B-grade partial-positive structural (substantive empirical fact + structural identification + conditional theorem, no closed-form theorem-grade proof, no algorithmic content). **Thread 11 wraps**. **Next-action**: ESCALATE to user — Threads 1-11 all closed; OPEN_POSITIVE_TARGETS.md post-§P11 list does not pre-load a Thread 12 target. See `experiments/constructions/p11_ulam_line_cover/{p11_ulam_line_cover.py, p11_ulam_bounded.py, p11_alt_embeddings.py, p11_top_lines_quadratic_decomp.py, p11_lp_relaxation.py, p11_lp_dual_inspect.py, p11_lp_guided_greedy.py, p11_iterated_rounding.py, p11_milp_check.py, p11_hl_singular_series.py, p11_hl_distribution_analysis.py, p11_hl_singular_series_results.md, hl_singular_series_results.csv, lp_summary_*, milp_*, iter_round_*}`, `archive/sessions/{session484_*, session485_*, session486_*, session487_*, session488_commit_thread11_hl_theoretical_wrap.md}`. | 